  "interpretation": [
    "Llama direction signs improve31/40 versus26/40 numeric; Qwen3 improves28/40 versus25/40; Qwen72 is25/40 in both tasks.",
    "Llama and Qwen3 each have5 classification-correct/numeric-incorrect cases;4/5 occur at direction-blocking endpoints and1/5 are unblocked.",
    "On unblocked signed trials, Llama classification is27/34 versus26/34 numeric, Qwen3 is24/36 versus25/36 numeric, and Qwen72 is25/40 in both tasks.",
    "The observed positive net gains are concentrated in baseline-endpoint cases. Independent task elicitation and a single repeat do not isolate a causal mechanism.",
    "Qwen72 has3 classification-only successes and3 numeric-only successes, all unblocked. Llama has0 numeric-only successes and Qwen3 has2, both unblocked.",
    "All5 classification-only successes in each of Llama and Qwen3 have numeric baselines at0 or1. The one unblocked case per model is a positive target starting at0, where an upward update remains possible.",
    "Direction-only forecasts still miss9 to14 of20 paired reversals and13 to18 of20 broken-link unchanged targets across models; endpoint relief does not account for all task failures.",
    "These descriptive development comparisons retain all planned denominators and do not replace the original probability protocol."
